  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, relays a history told by a lawyer named Dan Sheehan about US spying in the 1940s. According to Sheehan's account, after the OSS, the wartime US intelligence service, was wound down, the CIA, the US foreign intelligence agency, was formed at the urging of Brown Brothers Harriman, a private investment firm. If true, it would mean private financial interests shaped the agency from the start, which matters to those who think such interests also guard UFO secrets."
